*** Resetting replication at the very beginning of the test.

*** Generating a configuration file in JSON format for the Binlog
*** Server utility.

*** Determining binlog file directory from the server.

*** Creating a temporary directory <BINSRV_STORAGE_PATH> for storing
*** binlog files downloaded via the Binlog Server utility.

*** Determining the first binary log name.

*** Creating a table, filling it, rotating, and adding more rows.
CREATE TABLE t1(id INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT, PRIMARY KEY(id)) ENGINE=InnoDB;
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(DEFAULT);
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(DEFAULT);

*** Determining the second binary log name.

*** Starting Binlog Server Utility in background in pull mode.

*** Waiting for the replication source listener port ready to accept
*** connections.

*** Starting mysqlbinlog --read-from-remote-server --raw --stop-never
*** against PBS.

*** Restarting the source gracefully: the second binary log ends with
*** a STOP event, and the source starts the third one.
# restart

*** Determining the third binary log name.

*** Waiting for PBS to switch to the third binary log.

*** Waiting for the client to copy the second binary log completely
*** (up to and including the STOP event).

*** Letting the client move into the third binary log while PBS still
*** holds only its magic.

*** Adding rows and rotating: PBS writes the third binary log.
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(DEFAULT);
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;

*** Determining the fourth binary log name.

*** Adding rows and rotating once more, so that the fourth binary log
*** is closed as well.
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(DEFAULT);
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;

*** Waiting for the client to copy the fourth binary log completely.

*** Sending SIGTERM to the mysqlbinlog client and waiting for it to
*** terminate.

*** Comparing the client's copies of the closed binary logs with the
*** source's ones.
first binary log: identical
second binary log: identical
third binary log: identical
fourth binary log: identical

*** Dropping the table.
DROP TABLE t1;

*** Sending SIGTERM signal to the Binlog Server Utility and waiting
*** for the process to terminate.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility storage directory.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility log file.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility configuration file.
